Relevant tables, columns, and typical filters

numbers  
• `submission_number`: join key to submission  
• `measure_tag`: identify revenue facts – filter IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')  
• `number_of_quarters`: keep only 4‑quarter (annual) facts – filter = 4  
• `value`: dollar amount to aggregate (÷ 1 000 000 000 to show billions)  
• `units`: normally 'USD'; may add filter units='USD' (optional)

submission  
• `submission_number`: join key to numbers  
• `fiscal_year`: filter = 2016  
• `stprba`: U.S. state of business address – exclude NULL or ''  
• (optionally `form` = '10‑K' or '10‑Q', but not required)

Typical conditions  
• numbers.number_of_quarters = 4  
• numbers.measure_tag IN (…)  
• submission.fiscal_year = 2016  
• submission.stprba IS NOT NULL AND submission.stprba <> ''  

Ten exploratory → final SQLs  
(each ends with LIMIT 20 for sampling / result‑checking)

```sql
-- 1. Inspect distinct revenue‑type tags in the numbers table
SELECT DISTINCT measure_tag
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.numbers`
WHERE LOWER(measure_tag) LIKE '%revenue%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Quick look at states (stprba) that exist in 2016 submissions
SELECT DISTINCT stprba
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission`
WHERE fiscal_year = 2016
  AND stprba IS NOT NULL
  AND stprba <> ''
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Sample annual (4‑quarter) revenue facts for FY‑2016 filers
SELECT n.submission_number, n.measure_tag, n.value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.numbers` AS n
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` AS s
  ON n.submission_number = s.submission_number
WHERE s.fiscal_year = 2016
  AND n.number_of_quarters = 4
  AND n.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Same as #3 but add USD filter and show the state
SELECT s.stprba, n.measure_tag, n.value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.numbers`  AS n
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` AS s
  ON n.submission_number = s.submission_number
WHERE s.fiscal_year = 2016
  AND n.number_of_quarters = 4
  AND n.units = 'USD'
  AND n.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
  AND s.stprba IS NOT NULL AND s.stprba <> ''
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Aggregate total revenue (in dollars) by state for FY‑2016
SELECT s.stprba AS state, SUM(n.value) AS total_revenue_usd
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.numbers`  AS n
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` AS s
  ON n.submission_number = s.submission_number
WHERE s.fiscal_year = 2016
  AND n.number_of_quarters = 4
  AND n.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
  AND s.stprba IS NOT NULL AND s.stprba <> ''
GROUP BY state
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Convert to billions and order descending
SELECT s.stprba AS state,
       SUM(n.value)/1e9 AS revenue_billions
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.numbers`  AS n
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` AS s
  ON n.submission_number = s.submission_number
WHERE s.fiscal_year = 2016
  AND n.number_of_quarters = 4
  AND n.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
  AND s.stprba IS NOT NULL AND s.stprba <> ''
GROUP BY state
ORDER BY revenue_billions DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Check the contribution of the largest individual filing per state
SELECT s.stprba AS state, n.submission_number,
       SUM(n.value)/1e9 AS filing_revenue_billions
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.numbers`  AS n
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` AS s
  ON n.submission_number = s.submission_number
WHERE s.fiscal_year = 2016
  AND n.number_of_quarters = 4
  AND n.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
  AND s.stprba IS NOT NULL AND s.stprba <> ''
GROUP BY state, n.submission_number
ORDER BY filing_revenue_billions DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Include company name for context
SELECT s.stprba AS state, s.company_name,
       SUM(n.value)/1e9 AS company_revenue_billions
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.numbers`  AS n
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` AS s
  ON n.submission_number = s.submission_number
WHERE s.fiscal_year = 2016
  AND n.number_of_quarters = 4
  AND n.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
  AND s.stprba IS NOT NULL AND s.stprba <> ''
GROUP BY state, s.company_name
ORDER BY company_revenue_billions DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Verify that all facts are point‑in‑time (qtrs=4) and USD
SELECT DISTINCT n.number_of_quarters, n.units
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.numbers`  AS n
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` AS s
  ON n.submission_number = s.submission_number
WHERE s.fiscal_year = 2016
  AND n.number_of_quarters = 4
  AND n.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL – highest‑revenue state (billions) for FY‑2016
SELECT state,
       revenue_billions
FROM (
  SELECT s.stprba AS state,
         SUM(n.value)/1e9 AS revenue_billions,
         RANK() OVER (ORDER BY SUM(n.value) DESC) AS rk
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.numbers`  AS n
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` AS s
    ON n.submission_number = s.submission_number
  WHERE s.fiscal_year = 2016
    AND n.number_of_quarters = 4
    AND n.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
    AND s.stprba IS NOT NULL AND s.stprba <> ''
  GROUP BY state
)
WHERE rk = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

Running query 10 returns the U.S. state with the highest summed annual revenue (in billions) for fiscal‑year 2016 under the stated constraints.
